<title>USA: Zapata Corp Q1 shr $0.07 vs $0.48.</title>
<headline>Zapata Corp Q1 shr $0.07 vs $0.48.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In millions, expect per share)</p>
<p>						 1997		    1996</p>
<p> Revenues				   $ 26.0		 $ 23.9</p>
<p> Net income to common stockholders     1.9		   14.3</p>
<p>Per share data:</p>
<p>  Income from continuing operations   0.07		   0.02</p>
<p>  Income from discontinued operations   --		   0.44</p>
<p> Cululative effect of accounting change --		   0.02</p>
<p>  Net income per share		    0.07		   0.48</p>
<p>Average common shares and</p>
<p>   equivalents outstanding		29.6		   29.6</p>
<p>NOTE: Zapata's 1996 results included net income from discontinued operations of $13.2 million, or $0.44 per share, that resulted from the sale of the company's natural gas compression assets.</p>
<p>Also, the company in 1995 changed its method for reporting its equity in one of its holdings (Envirodyne Industries Inc) from a concurrent to a three-month delayed basis. That change resulted in a $0.02 per share for the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
